t_ms": 56985, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FNWhgpYFMdq3fdz14QCikB", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56985, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FNWhgpYFMdq3fdz14QCikB", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 59441, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01ExVLmUX93tbp9iPkLgFEvy", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59741, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ExVLmUX93tbp9iPkLgFEvy", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59741, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ExVLmUX93tbp9iPkLgFEvy", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64552, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were marked unhealthy, so neither was a valid target.\n  - The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n  - I ran the rollback again and it finished in all regions. I then checked the service status to confirm the result.\n- **Incident:** The request to open INC-0001 timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had been created, so I didn't submit it again and the on-call engineer was paged only once. It describes the bad v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the recovery.\n\n**Still needed:** someone should find out why v2.3.1 failed and what caused the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KFLbVtv3c3hXtcC2WjgHu7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UopCqJrY1EvmYcxzyHBGfC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). Both later releases, v2.3.1-rc (seq 2) and v2.3.1 (seq 3), are unhealthy. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PAitUKztALbQAm3kMCuWRE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01F5U1mBga9Twey9gP77H26K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. Rolling back to a known healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YMpMjhMwEZS26kPDvbRASX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AGeERzXHrqsizJyBotiPYS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P8eqXUT1hVJkTdrikQ5LGA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FNWhgpYFMdq3fdz14QCikB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api started failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Error rate was 0.18 and the service was unhealthy. The release history lists v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 as unhealthy; the most recent healthy release is v2.3.0. I rolled back to v2.3.0. The first attempt partially failed: the orchestrator error stopped the rollout after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback to v2.3.0 in all regions. After the rollback, all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.002. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may have been created anyway. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ExVLmUX93tbp9iPkLgFEvy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were marked unhealthy, so neither was a valid target.\n  - The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n  - I ran the rollback again and it finished in all regions. I then checked the service status to confirm the result.\n- **Incident:** The request to open INC-0001 timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had been created, so I didn't submit it again and the on-call engineer was paged only once. It describes the bad v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the recovery.\n\n**Still needed:** someone should find out why v2.3.1 failed and what caused the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}